00:51:09.300 --> 00:51:26.019
and these dynamics that form, yeah, I wanted to investigate that and really be honest and really hold those parts of myself to account and the narcissism of a middle-aged guy who is trying to, in his 50s, there's that ego death of maybe your career has cooled.
这些形成的动力，是的，我想对此进行调查，说实话，真正对自己的这些部分负责，以及一个中年人的自恋，他试图在 50 多岁的时候，也许你的职业生涯已经冷却了，自我死亡。

00:51:26.019 --> 00:51:28.059
Who are you without career definition?
如果没有职业定义，你是谁？

00:51:28.059 --> 00:51:30.260
I think that's another thing we don't know how to talk about.
我认为这是另一件事我们不知道如何谈论。

00:51:30.260 --> 00:51:37.420
We don't know how to talk about disability and we don't know how to talk about who are we, besides success, besides achievement, especially men, who are we?
我们不知道如何谈论残疾，我们不知道如何谈论我们是谁，除了成功，除了成就，尤其是男人，我们是谁？

00:51:37.420 --> 00:51:40.280
Like, who are we underneath the things we're chasing?
比如，在我们所追逐的事物之下，我们是谁？

00:51:40.280 --> 00:51:49.199
And yeah, I always felt like when in doubt, make sure to come the hardest at the character closest to me.
是的，我总是觉得当有疑问时，一定要对最接近我的角色采取最严厉的态度。

00:51:49.199 --> 00:51:55.360
And when in doubt, the characters who bear some resemblance to the members of my family, make them the heroes.
当有疑问时，那些与我的家人有些相似的人物，让他们成为英雄。

00:51:55.360 --> 00:51:59.679
But, and that's not, I'm not doing that just not to get yelled at.
但是，事实并非如此，我这样做并不是为了不被骂。

00:51:59.679 --> 00:52:03.760
I'm doing that because it's the most interesting to me.
我这样做是因为这对我来说是最有趣的。

00:52:03.760 --> 00:52:04.840
It's the most interesting to me.
这对我来说是最有趣的。

00:52:04.840 --> 00:52:10.960
