00:52:30.800 --> 00:52:32.599
And that's the big twist of the book.
这就是这本书的大转折。

00:52:32.599 --> 00:52:38.320
We talk about the cliff when we talk about young adults with a disability, but every character in this book is on a cliff.
当我们谈论残疾年轻人时，我们谈论悬崖，但这本书中的每个角色都处于悬崖之上。

00:52:38.320 --> 00:52:41.480
All of the characters are standing on some type of life cliff.
所有的角色都站在某种类型的人生悬崖上。

00:52:41.480 --> 00:52:46.679
And we all act like, ah, there's this one character that we have a label, there's this one person we have a label for.
我们都表现得好像，啊，我们有一个角色，我们有一个标签，有一个人，我们有一个标签。

00:52:46.679 --> 00:52:48.320
We know they have a disability.
我们知道他们有残疾。

00:52:48.320 --> 00:52:52.320
We can say they're going to have challenges in life because we have a term we're putting on it.
我们可以说他们在生活中会遇到挑战，因为我们有一个术语。

00:52:52.320 --> 00:52:55.119
No, we all have challenges.
不，我们都有挑战。

00:52:55.119 --> 00:53:11.119
Whether there's a term or not to put on our own version of our challenges, whether it's considered a disability or not, we are all just as fragile and just as strong as anybody else, we're all the same and everybody is on some type of cliff.
无论是否有一个术语来描述我们自己面临的挑战，无论它是否被视为残疾，我们都和其他人一样脆弱和坚强，我们都是一样的，每个人都处于某种悬崖上。

00:53:11.119 --> 00:53:22.639
And once we realize that, maybe then we know how to talk about disability, which is to say we are all working on challenges and we are all people first and no label can explain anybody away.
一旦我们意识到这一点，也许我们就知道如何谈论残疾，也就是说，我们都在应对挑战，我们都是以人为本，没有任何标签可以解释任何人。

00:53:22.639 --> 00:53:41.070
We're all sitting there on in some sort of, and at some sort of inflection point in our life, we all have these moments in our life where we have to figure shit out and evolve, and it doesn't matter what terminology or diagnosis we put on ourselves, we're all the same, we all have the same challenges, really.
我们都坐在生命中的某种转折点上，我们都会有这样的时刻，我们必须解决问题并不断发展，无论我们对自己使用什么术语或诊断，我们都是一样的，我们都面临着同样的挑战，真的。

